      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>There's a link below the text editor, itself, that says to \"Switch to plain text editor\". If you hit that, it will show you the HTML tags that Google Docs includes. In the case of the example you shared above, it has:<br />\r\n<em>&lt;b id=\"docs-internal-guid-36fa8185-7fff-b042-c81d-575d719e457a\"&gt;</em></p>\r\n\r\n<p>It looks like Google Docs is including this HTML as a reference. For some reason it uses the \"bold\" tag (\"&lt;b&gt;\") and adds an \"id\" tag to it. :-(&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Hope that helps?&nbsp;</p>",
